  "uprn": "10094943041",
  "decision_date": "01/09/2023",
  "description": "Temporary change of use of an area of Gunnersbury Park for the staging of a two day music event to be held on 16th and 17th September 2023. Set-up from 4th September 2023 and clearance by 23rd September 2023. Including erection of associated temporary structures, ancillary concessions and facilities.",
  "site_name": "Sports Hub",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "08/09/2023",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": "W3 8LQ",
  "street_name": "Popes Lane",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major all other major developments",
  "lapsed_date": "31/08/2026",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The event is permitted between Monday 4th September 2023 and clearance by 23rd September 2023 inclusive of site construction and demolition.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (698-P-01-A, 698-P-02, 698-P-04-A, 698-P-05-A, 698-P-06-A, 698-P-07-A, 698-P-08-A and Waste Management Plan. Received: 9/6/2023. Planning, Design, Environment & Heritage Statement and Event Management Plan. Received: 28/6/2023. Technical Note - Impact on TfL services. Received: 14/7/2023. Sound Management Plan. Received: 24/7/2023. Technical Note - Cycling Parking. Received: 24/7/2023. Construction Traffic Management Plan. Received: 29/8/2023) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - The Delivery and Servicing Management Plan shall be carried out in accordance with the hereby approved Construction Traffic Management Plan, any alterations or amendments must be agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am to 8pm Monday to Sunday. Noisy works (defined as works which can be heard outside the boundary of the park) shall only take place between 8am to 6pm on Mondays to Sunday. \r\nNo vehicle movements shall take place outside of the hours 0800 to 2000 Monday - Sunday.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - The cycle storage units referred to in the approved plans shall be installed and made available for use prior to the first event and the spaces shall be available throughout the duration of the event.",
    "Condition : 6 - Floodlighting hereby approved shall only be operational 0800-23.30 and turned off at all other times, except for that required for security and safety purposes. Floodlighting will take into consideration the location of and proximity to local residential premises.",
    "Condition : 7 - The uses and operational structures hereby approved shall only be operational 12:00-23:00 for the duration of the permission.",
    "Condition : 8 - The applicant shall keep a photo record and site conditions report for the duration of the time limit specified in Condition 1, and on conclusion of the events hereby approved shall, make provision for the landowner to complete the necessary remediation to return the site to its pre-event state as a minimum (save for any wear and tear as identified in the lease agreement).",
    "Condition : 9 - The event shall be carried out in accordance with the sound management plan hereby approved, or such other protocol as agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority, and shall be carried out in accordance with the details set out in the submitted document and supporting information.",
    "Condition : 10 - The event shall be carried out in accordance with the events management documents pertaining to crowd management and staggered movements of guests contained within the Event Management Plan and Transport Assessment.",
    "Condition : 11 - The event shall be carried out in accordance with Waste Management Planhereby approved, any alterations or amendments must be agreed in writing with the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
